// An array element is addressed by an INTEGER.
//
// A string index into an `object[]` is not a key lookup: the store is
// lowered as an element offset, so `registry["one"] = 1` computed a wild
// address from the string pointer and wrote through it -- the program
// died with a segmentation fault (exit -11) instead of being refused.
//
// The READ side already refuses this shape ("expected 'an int index'");
// the STORE side has to refuse it the same way, or a program that only
// writes is the one that crashes.
// Expect: TypeMismatch: expected an int index, found a string

void main() {
    object[] registry = [];
    registry["one"] = 1;
    printline("unreachable");
}
